From: Radeon24 <Radeon24@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 18:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] usb: gadget: net2280: no Memory Write and Invalidate on the
 NET2282

On a FortiGate 100D (NET2282 on a conventional PCI bus, 64 byte cache
line), a sustained host-to-device transfer on a CDC NCM gadget with
the DMA engines ends with the OUT endpoint never completing a request
again: the DMA_ABORT that handle_ep_small() writes at the end of a
short OUT transfer stays pending (DMA_ENABLE does not drop, and the
abort bit still reads 1 once the channel paused), and the channel then
ignores the next DMA_START. The four slow aborts recorded all stopped
14016 bytes into their transfer, 219 cache lines.

The NET2280 databook (8.6, 8.7) ends an aborted or paused Memory Write
and Invalidate burst at the next cache line boundary. With the probe
writing PCIMSTCTL without DMA Memory Write and Invalidate Enable on
the NET2282 (0x300 instead of 0x700, PCI_COMMAND unchanged), the same
traffic ran on three boots, one of them cold, with no slow abort at
all, every transfer checksummed, at four to five times the PIO rate
host to device and twice device to host.

NET2282 only; the NET2280 and the USB338x are unchanged. Also report
the value written at probe time.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Radeon24 <Radeon24@users.noreply.github.com>
---
--- a/drivers/usb/gadget/udc/net2280.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/gadget/udc/net2280.c
@@ -3818,9 +3818,18 @@
 		dev->ep[i].dummy = td;
 	}
 
-	/* enable lower-overhead pci memory bursts during DMA */
+	/* enable lower-overhead pci memory bursts during DMA.
+	 * NET2282: Memory Write only, no Memory Write and Invalidate.  The
+	 * NET2280 databook (8.6, 8.7) ends an aborted or paused MWI burst
+	 * at the next cache line boundary.  On a NET2282 the DMA_ABORT of a
+	 * short OUT transfer was seen to stay pending, each time a multiple
+	 * of the 64 byte cache line into the transfer, and the OUT endpoint
+	 * then stopped completing requests; without MWI the same CDC NCM
+	 * traffic ran with no slow abort at all.
+	 */
 	if (dev->quirks & PLX_LEGACY)
-		writel(BIT(DMA_MEMORY_WRITE_AND_INVALIDATE_ENABLE) |
+		writel(((dev->quirks & PLX_2280) ?
+			BIT(DMA_MEMORY_WRITE_AND_INVALIDATE_ENABLE) : 0) |
 			/*
 			 * 256 write retries may not be enough...
 			   BIT(PCI_RETRY_ABORT_ENABLE) |
@@ -3841,6 +3850,9 @@
 			pdev->irq, base, dev->chiprev);
 	ep_info(dev, "version: " DRIVER_VERSION "; %s\n",
 		dev->enhanced_mode ? "enhanced mode" : "legacy mode");
+	if ((dev->quirks & (PLX_LEGACY | PLX_2280)) == PLX_LEGACY)
+		ep_info(dev, "net2282: dma %s, no memory write and invalidate, pcimstctl %08x\n",
+			use_dma ? "on" : "off", readl(&dev->pci->pcimstctl));
 	retval = device_create_file(&pdev->dev, &dev_attr_registers);
 	if (retval)
 		goto done;
